-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Herbert's Dummy Run
  Publisher   Mikro-Gen, 1985
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Herbert's Dummy Run (1985)(Mikro-Gen).z80
  MD5         b5570016396fc2ec823da33a2a095ba3

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Herbert, the other figures and most of the scenery painted in
              fuller colour: Herbert in a white nappy with pink skin, the
              balls in solid yellow, no outlines or shading, mirrored facings
              to match. Source: Enhanced colours: Jon Attree.

  Pace        original (+1.21% measured in JNext 1.1.104, 10 runs per scene,
              Enhanced)

  Changes     1.0: the clash fix, every moving figure a sprite. 1.1-1.2: an
              optional Enhanced colour set for the figures and scenery. 1.3:
              hand-painted touches by Jon Attree to Herbert and the balls.

  Note        Controls: Q and W move, Caps Shift jumps. Herbert's drawing code
              is the same family as Everyone's a Wally and Three Weeks in
              Paradise, so this patch builds on theirs. Plays at the
              original's pace.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Partial immunity
   3  Working torch
   4  Loaded pop gun
   5  Loaded catapult
   6  Real ten pence
   7  Remove moving enemies

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

